    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1356">

                <pb facs="1333" n="1323" xml:id="pg1323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/8–3149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Nanking</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-31T14:00:00-04:00">August 31, 1949—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1038. ReDeptels 1028 to Nanking and 1727 to Shanghai Aug 26.<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d1356-f1"/> It is Dept’s intention and hope Emb and ConGen can
                    arrange for all departing personnel use first available transportation. Every
                    effort shld be made get personnel departing aboard <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>. If Dept has not issued trans orders for personnel
                    transferring, Nanking shld issue evacuation TO’s and inform Dept nr, date, names
                    of employees and families and destination evacuation TO’s.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking rptd Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
